# SwiftUI previews

Each view ships a `#Preview` in the **same file**, building a `Store` with overridden dependencies so
the preview is deterministic and needs no live data.

```swift
#Preview {
    HomeView(
        store: Store(initialState: HomeFeature.State()) {
            HomeFeature()
        } withDependencies: {
            $0.platformInfo.platformName = { "Preview" }
        }
    )
}
```

## Rules

- Colocate the preview with the view; no separate `*Preview.swift`.
- Override dependencies in the preview's `Store` (never hit the live value).
- Provide a useful state (default / loading / error) when the screen has meaningful variants.
- Use `:Styleguide` tokens/components in previews; reusable components in `:Styleguide` also ship a `#Preview`.
